<title>EGYPT: Egypt raises Giza 86 cotton export price.</title>
<headline>Egypt raises Giza 86 cotton export price.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian exporters raised overall prices for the Giza 86 cotton variety by one centilibre (U.S. cents per pound), the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association said on Monday.</p>
<p>The association said prices for all other grades and varieties were unchanged from last week. Prices are valid until 2200 GMT on October 12, 1996.</p>
<p>Prices, in centilibres, for the eight varieties (last week's prices in brackets)-</p>
<p>	   FG/EX   FG+1/4   FG	FG-1/4   G/FG   G+3/8   G+1/4</p>
<p>Giza 76  171.0   165.0    159.0   153.0    147.0  144.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 70  164.0   158.0    152.0   146.0    140.0  137.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 77  159.0   153.0    147.0   141.0    135.0  132.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 86  136.0   130.0    124.0   118.0    112.0  109.0    --</p>
<p>	  (135.0   129.0    123.0   117.0    111.0  108.0    --)</p>
<p>Giza 75  134.0   128.0    122.0   116.0    110.0  107.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 85  131.0   125.0    119.0   113.0    107.0  104.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 83  127.0   121.0    115.0   109.0    103.0  100.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 80  127.0   121.0    115.0   109.0    103.0  100.0    --</p>
<p>Note: FG/EX = fully good/excellent, G/FG = good/fully good</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/91</p>
</text>
